{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>so that his heart not be lifted above his brothers.</b> This is the giving of reason for 'silver and gold he shall not multiply to himself.'" "<b>and so as not to turn aside from the commandment</b> — this is the giving of reason for 'and he shall write for himself a copy of this Torah,' [namely] a Torah scroll that hangs on his arm and goes out and comes in with him. And I have heard that that Torah scroll which hangs on his arm had written in it nothing but the Ten Commandments. And since from אנכי to לרעך there are 613 letters, corresponding to the 613 commandments, it is called a Torah scroll."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:01:03.907552889Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}